@startuml
!include _style.puml
title Login and Server-Side Session Cookie
autonumber
actor "Guest" as Guest
participant "Next.js\nauth route" as Next
participant "Spring Security\nLoginRateLimitFilter" as Security
participant "AuthController" as API
participant "AuthServiceImp" as Auth
participant "PasswordService /\nJwtTokenService" as Credentials
database "UserRepository /\nAuthSessionRepository" as DB

Guest -> Next : POST /api/auth/login\n{usernameOrEmail, password}
note over Guest, Next
Middleware checks the request origin for API mutations.
Invalid JSON returns 400; upstream failures return 503.
end note
Next -> Security : POST /api/auth/login\nJSON credentials
alt Sixth request from the same backend source within default 60s window
  Security --> Next : 429 + Retry-After
  Next --> Guest : Login error; no new cookie
else Request admitted (default maximum: 5)
  Security -> API : @Valid Login request
  API -> Auth : loginWithUser(usernameOrEmail, password)
  Auth -> DB : findByUsername(identifier)\nfindByEmail(identifier)
  DB --> Auth : matching User records
  alt Missing/ambiguous identifier, inactive user, or invalid password
    Auth -> Credentials : matches(password, passwordHash)\n[only after identifier/status checks]
    Credentials --> Auth : BCrypt match result
    Auth --> API : IllegalArgumentException
    API --> Next : 401 Invalid username or password
    Next --> Guest : Login error
  else ACTIVE user and BCrypt password matches
    Auth -> Credentials : matches(password, passwordHash)
    Credentials --> Auth : true
    Auth -> Credentials : issue(userId, now, now + 24h)
    Credentials --> Auth : signed JWT
    Auth -> DB : deleteByExpiresAtBefore(now)
    Auth -> DB : save AuthSession(SHA-256(token), user, expiresAt)
    Auth --> API : LoginResponse(token, user)
    API --> Next : 200 ApiResponse<LoginResponse>
    Next -> Next : validate token and allowed user role
    Next --> Guest : user data + Set-Cookie: auth_token\nHttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; 24h\nSecure in production
  end
end
note over Next, Security
The browser receives user data, not the JWT in JSON.
Later proxies read the cookie and forward Authorization: Bearer.
The rate limiter keys on backend remoteAddr, not forwarded headers.
end note
' Sources: frontend/src/app/api/auth/[action]/route.ts; frontend/src/middleware.ts
' Sources: backend/src/main/java/project/project/Controller/AuthController.java
' Sources: backend/src/main/java/project/project/Service/implement/AuthServiceImp.java; PasswordService.java; JwtTokenService.java
' Sources: backend/src/main/java/project/project/Filter/LoginRateLimitFilter.java
@enduml
